<title>USA: US weekly soybean crush 23,457,000 bushels - NOPA.</title>
<headline>US weekly soybean crush 23,457,000 bushels - NOPA.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>National Oilseed Processors Association weekly soybean crushings by reporting members (crushings/capacity in bu, soymeal exports in short tons):</p>
<p>			 05/14/97    05/07/97	Year-Ago</p>
<p> Crushings	 23,457,000  24,568,000    23,097,000</p>
<p> Meal Exports	  34,301	50,911	     N/A</p>
<p> Capacity-X	35,451,000  35,451,000    34,100,000</p>
<p> Capacity-Y	35,643,944  35,643,944	     N/A</p>
<p>X-Members reporting weekly. Y-Weekly reporters plus members reporting only monthly. N/A-Not Available. Totals may not agree due to rounding by NOPA. R-revised  </p>
<p>NOPA reported the following soybean crushings and capacity use by state for the week, with comparisons, in bushels:</p>
<p>    CRUSHINGS --   05/14/97    05/07/97     Year-Ago</p>
<p> Illinois	   4,111,000   3,505,000     4,728,000</p>
<p> Ind, Ky, Ohio    3,731,000   4,700,000     3,576,000</p>
<p> Southeast	  4,087,000   4,193,000     4,313,000</p>
<p> South Central    1,490,000   2,462,000     1,772,000</p>
<p> Southwest	  3,401,000   3,531,000     2,718,000</p>
<p> Iowa		 4,643,000   4,419,000     4,075,000</p>
<p> Minn,ND,SD,Mont  1,994,000   1,759,000     1,915,000</p>
<p> Total U.S.	23,457,000  24,568,000    23,097,000</p>
</text>
